---
The contracts in `src/` need no case to be checked: the runner generates
arguments that meet each `requires` and checks each `ensures` on every one. The
cases here pin down exact answers, which no contract states.
---
suite catalogue.paging

case "an empty catalogue has no pages" {
	expect pageCount(0, 20) == 0
}

case "a full last page needs no extra page" {
	expect pageCount(40, 20) == 2
}

case "one item over starts another page" {
	expect pageCount(41, 20) == 3
}

case "the first page starts at the beginning" {
	expect offset(1, 20) == 0
}

case "the third page skips two pages' worth" {
	expect offset(3, 20) == 40
}
